      "per_curiam": false,
      "sha1": "",
      "snippet": "\nMr. Justice Stewart,\nconcurring.\nIn 1963, this Court, in Ferguson v. Skrupa, 372 U. S. 726, purported to sound the death knell for the doctrine of substantive due process, a doctrine under which many-state laws had in the past been held to violate the Fourteenth Amendment. As Mr. Justice Black\u2019s opinion for the Court in Skrupa put it: \u201cWe have returned to the original constitutiona",
